From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:31:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: Let the PLL notifier wait for the PLL to
 settle

Some PLLs need a settling time after they report the lock before their
output may be used. The PLL notifier returns as soon as the lock bit is
set.

Add a delay_us field to struct ccu_pll_nb, waited after the lock, as
struct ccu_mux_nb has for its reparenting. It is zero for all current
users, so they are unchanged.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with the PLL_GPU0 notifier of the A733 on two
boards, see the next patch; not tested on the SoCs of the other users,
for which the delay stays 0.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu_common.c | 3 +++
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu_common.h | 1 +
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu_common.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu_common.c
index 248e58c9562d..e7a496d167a7 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu_common.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu_common.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/clk-provider.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/device.h>
 #include <linux/iopoll.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
@@ -96,6 +97,8 @@ static int ccu_pll_notifier_cb(struct notifier_block *nb,
 
 	ccu_helper_wait_for_lock(pll->common, pll->lock);
 
+	udelay(pll->delay_us);
+
 out:
 	return notifier_from_errno(ret);
 }
diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu_common.h b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu_common.h
index d9dc24ad5503..6027f59c8b7a 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu_common.h
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu_common.h
@@ -73,6 +73,7 @@ struct ccu_pll_nb {
 
 	u32	enable;
 	u32	lock;
+	u32	delay_us;	/* How many us to wait after the lock */
 };
 
 #define to_ccu_pll_nb(_nb) container_of(_nb, struct ccu_pll_nb, clk_nb)
